messages:
nina: quick sync 1: platform wants to canonicalize the route/tenant headers. currently we see a mix: `x-route`, `x-route-meta`, `x-rw-route`. they want one: `x-rw-route-v1`.

kevin: thanks. is the idea to change payload schema or just header name?

nina: both. new header will be a compact json blob: {"r":"team:42","q":"read"} instead of long fields. smaller bytes, easier to parse at edge.

liam: sdk implications: python currently exposes route as request.options.route_id. TS/golang just forward raw headers. we'll need to add a small translator in each client.

sora: telemetry folks: if clients send old headers we get duplicate attribution events. can we have the SDK send a reconciliation ping when it sees both shapes? sampling 0.005?

henry: suggestion: SDKs should 1) emit new header always when route info is present, 2) also keep old header for N releases, 3) emit telemetry event with low sampling and flag whether parse succeeded. event name: sdk.route_header.normalize.

kevin: breakdown for SDKs: python -> add sync + async middleware that sets header; ts -> add node/browser header mapper; go -> small RoundTripper wrapper. keep changes minimal and nonblocking.

nina: can we avoid JSON string-in-string cases? we've seen some customers send quoted json string ("{"r":"x"}"). recommend SDKs detect and unquote before double-encoding.

liam: TS example I'll add to PR:
```ts
function normalizeRouteHeader(headers: Record<string,string>) {
  const candidates = ['x-rw-route', 'x-route-meta', 'x-route'];
  let raw = '';
  for (const k of candidates) {
    if (headers[k]) { raw = headers[k]; break; }
  }
  if (!raw) return;
  // strip wrapping quotes
  if (raw.startsWith('"') && raw.endsWith('"')) raw = raw.slice(1,-1);
  try {
    const parsed = JSON.parse(raw);
    headers['x-rw-route-v1'] = JSON.stringify({r: parsed.route_id || parsed.r, q: parsed.policy || 'default'});
    emitSampledEvent('sdk.route_header.normalize', {from: 'old', parsed: 'true'});
  } catch (e) {
    // fallback: pass through as opaque string
    headers['x-rw-route-v1'] = raw;
    emitSampledEvent('sdk.route_header.normalize', {from: 'old', parsed: 'false'});
  }
}
```

henry: go will need to preserve case-insensitive header names. RoundTripper should merge into http.Header canonical keys. also log length of encoded header for batching heuristics.

kevin: release plan proposal: 1) open PRs in all SDKs with feature flag ENV RW_HEADER_MODE=canary|stable|off. 2) produce canary releases with tag canary-header-normalize. 3) platform flips to dual-write for 1 week. 4) set default to stable in SDKs; old header removed in 60 days.

nina: timeline ok but we must add console telemetry tile to monitor quota misattribution before we flip. @sora can you own that?

sora: yep I'll add a tile: sample events vs inferred route counts, and a small alert if mismatch > 0.5% for 10m.

liam: tests: unit for normalization + e2e that runs canary SDK against staging platform dual-write. add integration test for quoted-json edge case.

henry: docs: deprecation notice + migration guide. include snippet for users who set route via SDK vs raw header. show how to opt-out with RW_HEADER_MODE=off.

deploy-bot: canary pipeline started for sdk-ts @ 1733333301 :rocket:
deploy-bot: sdk-ts-canary published -> 2.4.0-canary-header-normalize

kevin: I'll open the go PR today, land ts tomorrow, python Friday. keep PR descriptions consistent (what feature flag, telemetry sampling rate, test coverage).

nina: one more: telemetry schema change needs a minor bump. keep sampling default low (0.005) but allow opt-in via config for customers to increase.

liam: ack. I'll update the devex checklist with TODOs: PRs, canary releases, console tile, support playbook, deprecation email.

henry: thumbs up. everyone who owns an SDK react with :thumbsup: when your PR lands.
